# UI descriptions are static data. This library deliberately has no renderer.
# All section patterns and the descriptor representation are editable here.
import lib/sections.dl
import lib/callbacks.dl
import lib/check.dl

class:
    patterns:
        UI element
    members:
        kind as an integer
        text as a C string
        color as a C string
        columns as an integer
        rows as an integer
        border as an integer
        children as a pointer to a pointer to UI element
        count as an integer
        action as a pointer
        left as an integer
        top as an integer
        width as an integer
        height as an integer
        variant as a C string

UI reference means: a pointer to UI element
default UI cell width means: 220
default UI cell height means: 48
no UI children means: @intrinsic("construct", UI reference array of 0 items)
UI children of values means: @intrinsic("cast", a static reference to values, a pointer to UI reference)
no UI action means: @intrinsic("construct", a pointer)

UI node {integer:kind} with {C string:text} colored {C string:color} sized {integer:columns} by {integer:rows} bordered {integer:border} containing {an array:children} acting {a pointer:action} at {integer:left} {integer:top} measuring {integer:width} by {integer:height} styled {C string:variant} means: a static reference to @intrinsic("construct", UI element, kind, text, color, columns, rows, border, UI children of children, the length of children, action, left, top, width, height, variant)
UI node {integer:kind} with {C string:text} colored {C string:color} sized {integer:columns} by {integer:rows} bordered {integer:border} containing {an array:children} acting {a pointer:action} means: UI node kind with text colored color sized columns by rows bordered border containing children acting action at 0 0 measuring 0 by 0 styled ""
a UI container of kind {integer:kind} containing {an array:children} means: UI node kind with "" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing children acting no UI action

button {C string:label} means: UI node 2 with label colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
col {C string:label} means: UI node 5 with label colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
label {C string:text} means: UI node 11 with text colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action

implicitly convert {C string:label}:
    replacement:
        col label

section window {name}:
    declares: name
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 0 with name colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

section toolbar:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 1 with "" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

section {integer:columns} x {integer:rows} table:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 3 with "" colored "" sized columns by rows bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

section {C string:color} row:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 4 with "" colored color sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

section style:
    result: UI reference
    body:
        children: many UI reference
    value:
        UI node 6 with "" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing the body's children acting no UI action

tables are {C string:color} means: UI node 7 with "" colored color sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
table cells are {integer:width} x {integer:height} pixels means: UI node 8 with "" colored "" sized width by height bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
buttons are {C string:color} and have a {integer:width} [pixel|pixels] border means: UI node 9 with "" colored color sized 0 by 0 bordered width containing no UI children acting no UI action

class:
    patterns:
        UI handler
    members:
        target as UI reference
        action as a pointer
        next as a pointer to UI handler
        event as an integer

class:
    patterns:
        UI value
    members:
        target as UI reference
        text as a string
        number as an integer
        next as a pointer to UI value

class:
    patterns:
        UI instance
    members:
        description as UI reference
        state as a pointer
        status as a string
        handlers as a pointer to UI handler
        values as a pointer to UI value
        page as UI reference
        reduced motion as a boolean

this window means: @intrinsic("receiver")

section code:
    receiver: a pointer to UI instance
    returns: nothing
    result: UI reference
    value:
        UI node 10 with "" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting @intrinsic("cast", @intrinsic("deferred body"), a pointer)

section when the {C string:label} button is clicked:
    receiver: a pointer to UI instance
    returns: nothing
    value:
        bind the button labeled label in this window to @intrinsic("deferred body")

to get the UI child at {integer:index} in {UI reference:parent}:
    return the item at index in (parent's children)

# Tree lookup is independent of the concrete section patterns above.
to get the element of kind {integer:kind} labeled {C string:label} in {UI reference:root}:
    if root's kind = kind and root's text = label:
        return root
    set index to 0
    loop while index < root's count:
        set found to the element of kind kind labeled label in (the UI child at index in root)
        if found != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
            return found
        increment index
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)

to get the {C string:label} button in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set found to the element of kind 2 labeled label in (instance's description)
    if found = @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
        abort the program
    return found

the {C string:label} button means: the label button in this window

to bind the button labeled {C string:label} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance} to {a callback:action}:
    set target to (the label button in instance)
    set handler to @intrinsic("construct", UI handler, target, @intrinsic("cast", action, a pointer), instance's handlers, 0)
    set instance's handlers to storage for one slot initialized with handler

to initialize {a pointer to UI instance:instance} from {UI reference:node}:
    if node's kind = 10:
        @intrinsic("call pointer", node's action, nothing, instance)
    set index to 0
    loop while index < node's count:
        initialize instance from (the UI child at index in node)
        increment index

to get an instance of {UI reference:description} with state {a pointer to a value:state}:
    set result to a new UI instance
    set result's description to description
    set result's state to @intrinsic("cast", state, a pointer)
    set result's status to "Ready"
    initialize the address of result from description
    return result

to click {UI reference:button} in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set handler to instance's handlers
    loop while handler != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
        if handler's target = button:
            @intrinsic("call pointer", handler's action, nothing, instance)
            return nothing
        set handler to handler's next

to click the {C string:label} button in {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    click (the label button in instance) in instance

to close {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set handler to instance's handlers
    loop while handler != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
        set next to handler's next
        deallocate handler
        set handler to next
    set instance's handlers to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler)
    set value to instance's values
    loop while value != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI value):
        set next to value's next
        destroy the value at value
        deallocate value
        set value to next
    set instance's values to @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI value)

class:
    patterns:
        UI selection
    members:
        element as UI reference
        root as UI reference

to get the table of {UI reference:root}:
    set found to the element of kind 3 labeled "" in root
    require condition (found != @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)) reporting "This UI description has no table"
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI selection, found, root)

{UI reference:root}'s table means: the table of root

to get the {C string:color} row of {UI selection:table}:
    set index to 0
    loop while index < table's element's count:
        set entry to the UI child at index in (table's element)
        if entry's kind = 4 and entry's color = color:
            return @intrinsic("construct", UI selection, entry, table's root)
        increment index
    abort the program
    return a new UI selection

to get the UI cell width in {UI reference:root}:
    set rule to the element of kind 8 labeled "" in root
    if rule = @intrinsic("construct", UI reference):
        return default UI cell width
    return rule's columns

to get the width of {UI selection:row}:
    return (the table of row's root)'s element's columns * (the UI cell width in (row's root))
